This project is an independent reimplementation inspired by the ideas and
public interfaces of `AercherC/dsh-remote` (MIT). No code from that project is
copied verbatim except where explicitly noted below; the architecture, pairing
model, and security behavior were redesigned.

Third-party components
----------------------

1. QR Code generator
   - Component: qrcode-generator (https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator)
   - License: MIT
   - Usage: vendored (unmodified UMD, MIT header retained) as
     `lib/qrcode-generator.js`. The host generates an SVG string and the
     settings page renders it as an `<img>` data URL. No network request and no
     remote QR service is used.

2. cloudflared
   - Component: Cloudflare cloudflared (https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared)
   - License: Apache-2.0
   - Usage: downloaded at runtime (pinned version + SHA-256 verified) only when
     the user explicitly starts the Quick Tunnel transport. It is executed as a
     separate process and is not bundled with this project.
